# Auto commit and push

After every **completed** user-requested project change:

1. Run `git status`, `git branch --show-current`, `git diff --stat`
2. If there are safe changes: `git add .` → `git commit -m "..."` → `git push` (no extra flags on commit)
3. **Terminal permissions (always)** — run `git commit`, `git pull`, and `git push` via Shell with `required_permissions: ["git_write", "all"]` on the first attempt. Do not run push/commit in the sandbox and retry only after failure; request permissions up front. Do not ask the user to approve terminal access manually unless the tool rejects the request.
4. **No co-author trailers** — never use `git commit --trailer`, `--trailer "Co-authored-by: ..."`, or any `Co-authored-by:` line (including `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`). Commit with `git commit -m "message"` only — no `--trailer`, no multi-paragraph bodies, no co-author metadata.
5. Use conventional commit prefixes: `feat:`, `fix:`, `docs:`, `style:`, `refactor:`, `test:`, `chore:`, `build:`, `ci:`, `perf:`
6. Do **not** ask before commit/push unless: merge conflict, secrets at risk, push auth fails, protected branch, destructive command, unclear branch/remotes
7. Never run: `git commit --trailer`, `git reset --hard`, `git clean -fd`, `git push --force`, `git push --force-with-lease`, `git rebase`, `git branch -D`, `git branch -d`
8. No upstream: `git push -u origin $(git branch --show-current)`
9. Remote ahead: `git pull` then `git push`; on conflicts, stop and report files
10. No changes: say "No Git changes found, so nothing was committed or pushed."
11. Never commit `.env`, credentials, `node_modules/`, `target/`, session folders, or secrets from `application.yml`

On success, end with:

```
Done — committed and pushed to <branch>.

Commit: <message>
```
